From a4d31b46514e5ace1b2e5e1de5da5a3b43469b02 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 15:08:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] fix(cron): re-arm a restart rerun the host slept
 through; hold reruns out of DarkWakes

cron-7dfb141525: a MacBook asleep on battery woke only in DarkWakes; a restart cut
x-daily-post-and-engage, the immediate rerun was cut by the same sleep, and rerun-once
dropped the work although the host was then awake for hours.

- the owner stamps each cut attempt's awake (time.monotonic) and wall seconds
  (_run_clock beside _restart_cut, gateway/session_cron.py)
- a cut rerun with < 10 awake minutes (or asleep >= 10 min and most of the attempt) is
  re-armed, at most 3 reruns per original cut; unmeasured attempts keep rerun-once
- the due scan holds a pending restart rerun while macOS is not fully awake
  (pmset UserIsActive, or lid open on AC); the next scheduled slot settles a held rerun
- a held one-shot rerun is exempt from the one-shot grace gate: a DarkWake longer than
  ONESHOT_GRACE_SECONDS no longer retires the redone work as missed (review 5894188903)
